{
  "$schema": "../../schema/livery.schema.json",
  "id": "white-blue-1985",
  "airline": "BN1984",
  "name": "White over blue (1985)",
  "kind": "standard",
  "from": "1984-03",
  "to": "1989-11",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "drawnOn": "B722",
  "description": "The restarted Braniff's launch scheme, as worn by its 727-200s in 1985: a white body over a dark navy blue belly, the line between them straight and level along the body at about the wing root's height, with a pewter-silver line about 0.3 m deep along its top. Behind the wing the blue rises in a straight diagonal from under the side engines up across the tail cone, the center engine's fairing and the fin to the tailplane's fairing, so the fin's lower aft part, the rudder's foot and the tail cone are blue, the pewter line running on up along it. 'BRANIFF' in Braniff's red wordmark (heavy, slanted, extended capitals, each split by a thin white line a third of the way down) low on the forward body, its foot just on the pewter line, and again along the diagonal on the fin and fairing reading up toward the tail. White engine cowlings with polished lips, gray wings.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Braniff_Airways_Boeing_727-227;_N456BN,_November_1984_DCC_(5288412925).jpg",
      "title": "Braniff Airways Boeing 727-227 N456BN, November 1984 (CC BY-SA 2.0, Aero Icarus)",
      "accessed": "2026-11-24",
      "note": "727-200 N456BN, left side, side-on, high resolution, November 1984: every edge and both titles measured on it (fitted to shapes/B722.json with tools/photo_trace.py from the nose, the tail cone, the tailplane fairing's tip, the fin root, the crown and belly and the forward door, within 3-19 px at 5159 px wide)."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boeing_727-227(Adv),_Braniff_JP5920313.jpg",
      "title": "Boeing 727-227(Adv), Braniff (GFDL 1.2, Jon Proctor)",
      "accessed": "2026-11-24",
      "note": "727-200, left side, 1 December 1984, in good light: the pewter line over the blue along the body and under the fin's title, the colors, white engine cowlings."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:135_21-9-84_N466BN_Chicago_(54052529686).jpg",
      "title": "N466BN, Chicago, 21 September 1984 (CC BY-SA 2.0, Pete Macklin)",
      "accessed": "2026-11-24",
      "note": "727-200 N466BN, left side: a check of the diagonal's line from the fin down behind the side engine, and the titles."
    },
    {
